From 76ef22b930c96ff5d83cfbc0da320a485d46af7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:23:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: skip zero fills of never-used chunk pages; time vkd3d's
 transfers and the GPU work between render passes

New D3D12 memory vkd3d suballocates (buffers under 2 MB, textures and
heaps under 8 MB) gets a zero fill on the transfer queue, and every
queue waits for it. Each chunk now remembers which of its 64 KiB pages
were ever handed out; a suballocation only in pages never used since
vkAllocateMemory zeroed the chunk skips the fill when
VKD3D_FEX_SKIP_FRESH_CLEARS=1 (Turnip only; with
VK_EXT_zero_initialize_device_memory on, chunks are allocated with the
zero-initialize flag).

A new report (vkd3d_fex_gpu_report, 'FEXG') counts what new memory
needed (fresh, filled on GPU/CPU, skipped, not zeroed, own allocations,
chunks, WriteToSubresource uploads), the GPU and CPU time of every
transfer queue submission, and, in measured frames, how long each
command list waited for earlier GPU work and the GPU time between
render passes grouped by what the game recorded there.

Pass meter results are reset from the CPU once read, so a query pair
used again can't show its earlier use's timestamps before the GPU wrote
the new ones.
